{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Frc5TowdmDKtfVNZy5Bsnn","type":"tool_result","content":"{\r\n  \"id\": \"US-144\",\r\n  \"title\": \"Replace JavaScript tooltip positioning with CSS Popover API and Anchor Positioning\",\r\n  \"priority\": \"low\",\r\n  \"description\": \"The HTML Popover API (Baseline 2024) provides built-in keyboard navigation, Escape-key dismissal, focus management, and top-layer rendering without JavaScript. CSS Anchor Positioning (Chrome 125+) replaces Popper.js-style JavaScript tethering. Migrating hostel site tooltips and info-popovers to these native APIs reduces JS bundle size and provides accessible behaviour for free.\",\r\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\r\n    \"All tooltip and informational popover components use the popover HTML attribute and popovertarget button attribute instead of JavaScript show/hide logic\",\r\n    \"Popovers are tethered to their trigger using CSS anchor-name and position-anchor properties, not JavaScript position calculation\",\r\n    \"Keyboard test confirms: Tab reaches trigger, Enter/Space opens popover, Escape closes and returns focus to trigger, Tab navigates within popover\",\r\n    \"axe-core audit reports no new violations introduced by the migration\",\r\n    \"Bundle size (tracked in next build output) decreases by at least 2 KB after removing any Popper.js or equivalent dependency\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"technicalNotes\": [\r\n    \"Popover API: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Popover_API/Using \\u2014 use popover='auto' for light-dismiss behaviour\",\r\n    \"CSS Anchor Positioning: https://developer.chrome.com/docs/css-ui/anchor-positioning-api \\u2014 assign anchor-name on trigger, position-anchor on popover\",\r\n    \"Add @supports guard for browsers without anchor positioning; fall back to CSS position: absolute with manual offset\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"dependencies\": [],\r\n  \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\r\n  \"passes\": false,\r\n  \"model\": 