adata includes slug, title, excerpt, date, category, author, readTime, tags, featuredImage\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Content HTML must stay under 8000 characters for performance\r\n- All blog post fields are required; missing fields cause TypeScript compilation errors\r\n- Category must match existing categories or create new ones (checked against unique set)\r\n\r\n### Test results\r\n- Content size: 6,066 characters (well under 8,000 limit)\r\n- TypeScript compilation: ✓ passes (npx tsc --noEmit)\r\n- Next.js build: ✓ succeeds (67 static pages including new blog post)\r\n- Blog post accessible via /blog/singapore-work-pass-guide-malaysians slug\r\n- All acceptance criteria met:\r\n  - ✓ Slug and category correct\r\n  - ✓ Comparison table with all 3 pass types and salary minimums\r\n  - ✓ FAQ section with 5 Q&As (exceeds 3 required)\r\n  - ✓ ReadTime '12 min read', date '2026-04-14'\r\n  - ✓ npm run build passes\r\n\r\n## Iteration US-196 - Fri, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: Integrate channel manager for live OTA availability synchronisation (ID: US-196)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- **Beds24 client** (`site/src/lib/beds24-client.ts`):\r\n  - Implemented `parseAvailabilityResponse()` to parse real Beds24 API responses\r\n  - Returns proper `ChannelManagerAvailability` objects with room inventory\r\n  - Graceful fallback to placeholder data when channel manager is not configured\r\n- **ARI endpoint** (`site/src/app/api/ari/route.ts`):\r\n  - Fetches live availability from Beds24 API\r\n  - Maps to standard ARI format for connectivity partners (Google Free Booking Links)\r\n  - Returns JSON with property info, rooms, rates, and booking URL\r\n- **Booking sync endpoint** (`site/src/app/api/bookings/sync/route.ts`):\r\n  - Accepts POST requests with booking details (checkin, checkout, guest info, room type)\r\n  - Syncs bookings to Beds24 to close availability across OTAs\r\n  - Includes availability check via GET with query parameters\r\n- **Webhook endpoint** (`site/src/app/api/webhooks/beds24/route.ts`):\r\n  - Processes Beds24 webhook events for availability updates, booking creation/cancellation\r\n  - Validates webhook signature using HMAC-SHA256\r\n  - Logs event details (extensible for database updates)\r\n- **Configuration & types**:\r\n  - Channel manager config with environment variables\r\n  - Type definitions for availability, bookings, webhooks\r\n  - Updated .env.local.example with all required secrets\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Next.js App Router uses async GET/POST functions\r\n- Beds24 API response structure uses `roomtypes` key with room availability objects\r\n- Response parsing should handle multiple field names (id/roomId, name/roomName) for flexibility\r\n- Placeholder data allows testing without configured channel manager\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Beds24 API field names vary (id vs roomId, total vs totalInventory)\r\n- Parser must be defensive and return empty array on malformed responses\r\n- Webhook validation using HMAC requires exact payload matching (must use `request.text()` not `request.json()`)\r\n\r\n### Test results\r\n- TypeScript compilation: ✓ passes (npx tsc --noEmit)\r\n- Next.js build: ✓ succeeds (all 65 static pages generated)\r\n- ARI endpoint: ✓ shows as dynamic route (ƒ)\r\n- Webhook endpoint: ✓ shows as dynamic route (ƒ)\r\n- Booking sync endpoint: ✓ shows as dynamic route (ƒ)\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-196 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nThis user story is for a hotel channel manager integration, which seems mismatched with the `lhdn_payroll_integration` app context. The following brief assumes the target is a hospitality-focused Frappe app (e.g., `pelangi_hospitality`).\r\n\r\n**Project:** US-196: Channel Manager Integration\r\n**Target App:** `pelangi_hospitality` (Assumed)\r\n\r\n**1. Python Files to Modify:**\r\n*   **New File:** `pelangi_hospitality/api/channel_manager.py` to encapsulate all communication with the third-party channel manager API (e.g., Beds24).\r\n*   **New File:** `pelangi_hospitality/api/webhooks.py` to create a dedicated, whitelisted endpoint to receive incoming ARI updates and bookings from the channel manager.\r\n*   **Existing File:** `pelangi_hospitality/doctype/booking/booking.py` (or similar for reservations) to add logic that pushes new bookings to the channel manager.\r\n\r\n**2. Frappe DocTypes & Hooks:**\r\n*   **DocTypes:**\r\n    *   A new singleton `Channel Manager Settings` DocType is needed to store API keys, endpoint URLs, and credentials.\r\n    *   The `Booking` DocType will require modification to trigger syncs and store the channel manager's external booking ID.\r\n    *   The `Room` DocType needs a field to map its ID to the corresponding ID in the channel manager.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
