{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NqnR8iYAwteRsSzXNoxfEA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"use client\";\n2\t\n3\timport { useEffect, useState } from \"react\";\n4\timport type { Heading } from \"@/lib/headings\";\n5\t\n6\tinterface Props {\n7\t  headings: Heading[];\n8\t}\n9\t\n10\texport default function TableOfContents({ headings }: Props) {\n11\t  const [activeId, setActiveId] = useState<string>(\"\");\n12\t  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false);\n13\t\n14\t  useEffect(() => {\n15\t    if (headings.length === 0) return;\n16\t\n17\t    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(\n18\t      (entries) => {\n19\t        for (const entry of entries) {\n20\t          if (entry.isIntersecting) {\n21\t            setActiveId(entry.target.id);\n22\t            break;\n23\t          }\n24\t        }\n25\t      },\n26\t      { rootMargin: \"-20% 0% -70% 0%\" }\n27\t    );\n28\t\n29\t    headings.forEach(({ id }) => {\n30\t      const el = document.getElementById(id);\n31\t      if (el) observer.observe(el);\n32\t    });\n33\t\n34\t    return () => observer.disconnect();\n35\t  }, [headings]);\n36\t\n37\t  if (headings.length === 0) return null;\n38\t\n39\t  const items = (\n40\t    <ol className=\"space-y-1\">\n41\t      {headings.map(({ id, text, level }) => (\n42\t        <li key={id} style={{ paddingLeft: level === 3 ? \"1rem\" : \"0\" }}>\n43\t          <a\n44\t            href={`#${id}`}\n45\t            onClick={() => setIsOpen(false)}\n46\t            className={`block py-1 text-sm leading-snug transition-colors hover:text-amber-700 dark:hover:text-amber-400 ${\n47\t              activeId === id\n48\t                ? \"text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 font-medium\"\n49\t                : \"text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400\"\n50\t            }`}\n51\t          >\n52\t            {text}\n53\t          </a>\n54\t        </li>\n55\t      ))}\n56\t    </ol>\n57\t  );\n58\t\n59\t  return (\n60\t    <nav aria-label=\"Article table of contents\">\n61\t      {/* Mobile: collapsible accordion */}\n62\t      <div className=\"lg:hidden border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-700 rounded-xl overflow-hidden bg-white dark:bg-stone-800\">\n63\t        <button\n64\t          type=\"button\"\n65\t          onClick={() => setIsOpen(!isOpen)}\n66\t          className=\"w-full flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-200 hover:bg-stone-50 dark:hover:bg-stone-700 transition-colors\"\n67\t          aria-expanded={isOpen}\n68\t        >\n69\t          <span>Table of Contents</span>\n70\t          <svg\n71\t            className={`w-4 h-4 transition-transform ${isOpen ? \"rotate-180\" : \"\"}`}\n72\t            fill=\"none\"\n73\t            stroke=\"currentColor\"\n74\t            viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"\n75\t            aria-hidden=\"true\"\n76\t          >\n77\t            <path\n78\t              strokeLinecap=\"round\"\n79\t              strokeLinejoin=\"round\"\n80\t              strokeWidth={2}\n81\t              d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"\n82\t            />\n83\t          </svg>\n84\t        </button>\n85\t        {isOpen && (\n86\t          <div className=\"px-4 pb-4 pt-2 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-stone-700\">{items}</div>\n87\t        )}\n88\t      </div>\n89\t\n90\t      {/* Desktop: static list */}\n91\t      <div className=\"hidden lg:block\">\n92\t        <p className=\"text-xs font-semibold text-stone-400 uppercase tracking-wider mb-3\">\n93\t          On this page\n94\t        </p>\n95\t        {items}\n96\t      </div>\n97\t    </nav>\n98\t  );\n99\t}\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db47caa7-f1dd-496e-b0bd-79b00484628d","uuid":"94eceb51-2f79-4a8d-86e0-56748568d401","timestamp":"2026-04-14T00:11:41.865Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/c/Users/Jyue/Documents/1-projects/Software Projects/pelangi-website/site/src/components/TableOfContents.tsx","content":"\"use client\";\n\nimport { useEffect, useState } from \"react\";\nimport type { Heading } from \"@/lib/headings\";\n\ninterface Props {\n  headings: Heading[];\n}\n\nexport default function TableOfContents({ headings }: Props) {\n  const [activeId, setActiveId] = useState<string>(\"\");\n  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (headings.length === 0) return;\n\n    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(\n      (entries) => {\n        for (const entry of entries) {\n          if (entry.isIntersecting) {\n            setActiveId(entry.target.id);\n            break;\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      { rootMargin: \"-20% 0% -70% 0%\" }\n    );\n\n    headings.forEach(({ id }) => {\n      const el = document.getElementById(id);\n      if (el) observer.observe(el);\n    });\n\n    return () => observer.disconnect();\n  }, [headings]);\n\n  if (headings.length === 0) return null;\n\n  const items = (\n    <ol className=\"space-y-1\">\n      {headings.map(({ id, text, level }) => (\n        <li key={id} style={{ paddingLeft: level === 3 ? \"1rem\" : \"0\" }}>\n          <a\n            href={`#${id}`}\n            onClick={() => setIsOpen(false)}\n            className={`block py-1 text-sm leading-snug transition-colors hover:text-amber-700 dark:hover:text-amber-400 ${\n              activeId === id\n                ? \"text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 font-medium\"\n                : \"text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400\"\n            }`}\n          >\n            {text}\n          </a>\n        </li>\n      ))}\n    </ol>\n  );\n\n  return (\n    <nav aria-label=\"Article table of contents\">\n      {/* Mobile: collapsible accordion */}\n      <div className=\"lg:hidden border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-700 rounded-xl overflow-hidden bg-white dark:bg-stone-800\">\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          onClick={() => setIsOpen(!isOpen)}\n          className=\"w-full flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-200 hover:bg-stone-50 dark:hover:bg-stone-700 transition-colors\"\n          aria-expanded={isOpen}\n        >\n          <span>Table of Contents</span>\n          <svg\n            className={`w-4 h-4 transition-transform ${isOpen ? \"rotate-180\" : \"\"}`}\n            fill=\"none\"\n            stroke=\"currentColor\"\n            viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"\n            aria-hidden=\"true\"\n          >\n            <path\n              strokeLinecap=\"round\"\n              strokeLinejoin=\"round\"\n              strokeWidth={2}\n              d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"\n            />\n          </svg>\n        </button>\n        {isOpen && (\n          <div className=\"px-4 pb-4 pt-2 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-stone-700\">{items}</div>\n        )}\n      </div>\n\n      {/* Desktop: static list */}\n      <div className=\"hidden lg:block\">\n        <p className=\"text-xs font-semibold text-stone-400 uppercase tracking-wider mb-3\">\n          On this page\n        </p>\n        {items}\n      </div>\n    </nav>\n  );\n}\n","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":100}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BX5nks4gGQV7B7SKto2EpD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. There are no existing tooltip/popover libraries to remove. The codebase uses:\n\n1. `title=\"Search (Ctrl+K)\"` on the search button - native browser tooltip\n2. `useState`-based show/hide for overlays and menus (not really tooltips)\n3. No Popper.js, no floating-ui, no tippy.js\n\nThe story asks me to:\n1. Create components using the Popover API with `popover` attribute\n2. Use CSS anchor positioning for tethering\n3. Handle keyboard navigation properly\n4. Pass axe-core audit\n\n\n5. The 2KB bundle reduction is a red herring since there's nothing to remove\n\nSince this is a Next.js 16 / React 19 project with no tooltip library, I'll create a minimal `InfoPopover` component leveraging the native HTML `popover` attribute and `popovertarget`, style it with CSS anchor positioning and a `@supports` fallback, then apply it to a couple of places in the codebase where it makes sense—like replacing the `title` attribute on the search button. The key constraint is keeping the diff under 500 lines.\n\nMy plan: create the component (~60 lines), add the CSS for popover and anchor positioning (~30 lines), update the Header to use it (~15 lines), and mark the PRD as complete. That's roughly 120 lines total. Actually, wait—the acceptance criteria just requires that any tooltip or popover components use the native API instead of JavaScript logic. Since there are no existing components to replace, creating new ones that use the native popover API trivially satisfies this. The second criterion about popovers being tethered to their triggers using CSS anchor positioning I'll handle in the component's CSS. The native popover attribute and popovertarget button automatically handle keyboard interactions like Tab, Enter/Space, and Escape. As long as I use proper ARIA attributes, the accessibility audit should pass. Since there's no Popper.js dependency to remove, the bundle size criterion doesn't really apply here, but I'll note that. So I'll build the reusable InfoPopover component, add the necessary CSS styling and anchor positioning to globals.css, then swap out the title attribute in Header.tsx for the new component.\n\nLet me check what's already in globals.css before I start.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4790,"cache_read_input_tokens":42292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4790},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db47caa7-f1dd-496e-b0bd-79b00484628d","uuid":"53359b66-52fd-4950-b29e-8bbebd2f5978"}
